## CODE QUALITY

Even though speed matters, the code should still look like something a junior/mid-level Android developer would reasonably submit for a hiring assignment.

Use:

* meaningful names
* sensible separation of responsibilities
* lifecycle-safe code
* coroutines correctly
* no blocking work on the main thread
* proper permission handling
* no hardcoded sensitive information beyond demo credentials
* comments only where they actually help
* no unnecessary complexity

Avoid:

* giant god classes
* duplicated code
* deprecated APIs where a simple modern alternative exists
* fake implementations pretending to be face recognition
* TODOs in critical functionality

